{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GG5y57vY55mU5p5nr6rJCu","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","number":3345,"kind":"pr","title":"(fix) De-duplicate repeated lab results in the test results viewer","state":"merged","author":"cerveaubleu64","createdAt":"2026-05-29T10:02:16.000Z","mergedAt":"2026-06-10T06:24:55.000Z","closedAt":"2026-06-10T06:24:55.000Z","url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/pull/3345","mergeCommit":"16600fbfd85e41b98eaaa84817293a6b9e2af65f","syncedAt":"2026-10-23T19:00:04.598Z","tickets":[],"commits":[{"sha":"16600fbfd85e41b98eaaa84817293a6b9e2af65f","source":"merge-commit-sha","verified":true}],"files":[{"path":"packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.test.tsx","additions":150,"deletions":0},{"path":"packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx","additions":21,"deletions":16}],"body":"## Requirements\r\n\r\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/frontend-modules/contributing.en-US#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\r\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\r\n- [ ] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes a bug where lab results were displayed multiple times in the patient-chart lab results viewer. The root cause was that the de-duplication key used `flatName` instead of `conceptUuid`, causing the same observation to render once per order branch. The fix keys de-duplication on `conceptUuid` so identical observations (same concept + datetime + value) collapse into a single row.\r\n\r\n### Problem\r\n\r\nOn the patient-chart lab results viewer, a single lab result is rendered multiple times — once per order placed for that test. A NEW order plus its auto-generated DISCONTINUE order made the same result show twice; two orders, four times, and so on.\r\n\r\n### Root cause\r\n\r\nThe /obstree backend returns the same orderable-test concept under several branches of the orderable-tests tree (effectively one branch per order), each branch carrying the same single observation. In filter-context's tableData builder the de-duplication key is based on test.flatName, which differs per branch, so the identical observation is not collapsed and renders once per branch.\r\n\r\n### Fix\r\n\r\nKey the de-duplication on the observation's conceptUuid instead of flatName. The same observation (same concept + datetime + value) reached via different branches now collapses to a single row, while genuinely different tests stay separate. One-line change, no new dependencies, no new i18n keys.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n<!-- Required if you are making UI changes. -->\r\n\r\n## Related Issue\r\n<!-- Paste the link to the Jira ticket here if one exists. -->\r\n<!-- https://issues.openmrs.org/browse/O3- -->\r\n\r\n## Other\r\n<!-- Anything not covered above -->\r\n","comments":[{"kind":"review","author":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer","createdAt":"2026-06-01T15:12:48.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":"## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR fixes duplicated rows in the patient-chart lab results viewer by changing the table de-duplication key from `flatName` (branch-specific) to the test’s `conceptUuid` (concept identity), so the same observation returned under multiple /obstree branches collapses into a single rendered row.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Update table row de-duplication key generation to prefer `conceptUuid` over `flatName`.\n- Add inline rationale explaining why `flatName` caused duplicates with /obstree’s branching behavior.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>."},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer","createdAt":"2026-06-01T15:12:48.000Z","state":null,"path":"packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx","line":146,"body":"The new de-duplication behavior (keying by conceptUuid instead of flatName) isn’t covered by the existing filter-context unit tests. Without a targeted test case, regressions (e.g., reintroducing flatName-based keys) could slip in unnoticed.\n\nConsider adding a test where two different tree leaves have different flatName values but the same conceptUuid and identical obs (same obsDatetime + value), and assert that tableData contains only one entry for that observation."},{"kind":"review","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-06-02T20:24:09.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-06-02T20:24:10.000Z","state":null,"path":"packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx","line":145,"body":"Thanks for tackling this. On dev3, `/obstree` can return the same observation through multiple branches, so deduping is the right direction. I think this key is a bit too broad because it dedupes before we group rows by the rendered panel. The current CI failure shows this with the existing `mockResults` fixture: the Complete blood count panel, Platelets included, is mounted under two top-level roots, Hematology and Bloodwork, so the same observations appear under both. Keying only on concept identity keeps the first and drops the second, which reduces the tree view from 3 tables to 2 and the Platelets rows from 2 to 1. \r\n\r\nCould we scope the dedupe to the rendered group as well, for example include the group key derived from `flatName`, or dedupe after grouping? A focused regression test for this fixture shape would also help lock the intended behavior in."},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-06-10T05:02:02.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"@denniskigen could you re-review this? I missed this before and I think it would be good if we can get this in, if it looks good"},{"kind":"review","author":"jayasanka-sack","createdAt":"2026-06-10T06:24:13.000Z","state":"APPROVED","path":null,"line":null,"body":"Looks good to me, thanks @cerveaubleu64 and @NethmiRodrigo!"}],"nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aab9b392-fce1-445f-b705-57f814df3042","uuid":"dc1444ee-addd-4a97-a307-d08f0d579e6f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:10:05.558Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","number":3345,"kind":"pr","title":"(fix) De-duplicate repeated lab results in the test results viewer","state":"merged","author":"cerveaubleu64","createdAt":"2026-05-29T10:02:16.000Z","mergedAt":"2026-06-10T06:24:55.000Z","closedAt":"2026-06-10T06:24:55.000Z","url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/pull/3345","mergeCommit":"16600fbfd85e41b98eaaa84817293a6b9e2af65f","syncedAt":"2026-10-23T19:00:04.598Z","tickets":[],"commits":[{"sha":"16600fbfd85e41b98eaaa84817293a6b9e2af65f","source":"merge-commit-sha","verified":true}],"files":[{"path":"packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.test.tsx","additions":150,"deletions":0},{"path":"packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx","additions":21,"deletions":16}],"body":"## Requirements\r\n\r\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly des